We contrast two diametrically opposed problem-solving configurations:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Direct Adaptive Thinking (Diagnostic Stress Test):} The model receives an 81-character puzzle string representation (with empty cells marked as dots) and is prompted to deduce the solution directly.

We therefore deploy a dual evaluation design:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textit{Comprehensive 500-Puzzle Benchmark:} All 9 synthesized Python solvers and both energy-based formulations (learned CRAM across 3 random seeds and the hand-set Hopfield baseline) are evaluated exhaustively across all 500 benchmark instances, yielding 4,500 programmatic solver runs and 2,000 energy-based solver runs.

